{
  "name": "Add new SEC Form D funding raises to Google Sheets daily",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Add new SEC Form D funding raises to Google Sheets daily\n\n### Who it's for\nB2B sales teams, VC deal sourcing and funding newsletters who want companies that just raised money.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Schedule** fires on weekdays at 8:00.\n2. **Run SEC Form D New Raises Feed** pulls new Form D filings from SEC EDGAR via Apify. Funds are excluded and offerings are $1M+ by default; only filings not seen before (`stateKey`).\n3. **Has filings?** stops on empty days.\n4. **Pick columns** keeps the useful fields.\n5. **Append or update in Google Sheets** matches on `accessionNumber`.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Get your Apify API token: Apify Console > Settings > API & Integrations.\n2. In *Run SEC Form D New Raises Feed*, create a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`. Never paste the token into the URL or body.\n3. Connect your **Google Sheets** credential, paste your spreadsheet ID, and put the column names from *Pick columns* in row 1.\n4. Run once manually, check the output, then activate.\n\n### Customize the input\nEdit the JSON body of *Run SEC Form D New Raises Feed*: `states`, `industryGroups`, `minOfferingAmount`, `excludeFunds`, `lookbackDays`. Keep `stateKey` fixed so you only get new filings.\n\n### Requirements\nApify, pay per result: $0.01 per run + $0.005 per filing. Official SEC data, no personal names.\nActor: https://apify.com/cce_partners/sec-form-d-new-raises-feed\n\n### How to extend\nSend a Slack digest, enrich the company domain, or push rows to your CRM.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "3c060b13-50c4-4126-8e06-722f7e365e35",
      "name": "Overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Schedule\nChange the cron/interval here. Runs once per period; the Actor itself skips anything already sent.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "59b37fe6-26fe-4642-8cdc-4b2a4d146bad",
      "name": "Step 1: Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Run SEC Form D New Raises Feed on Apify\nPOST to run-sync-get-dataset-items with your filters in the JSON body. Auth: your Header Auth credential (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`). Timeout 300 s.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "e02541b9-9aad-4f8b-aa60-e35d97d26a5e",
      "name": "Step 2: Run the Actor",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Filter and deliver to Google Sheets\n*Has filings?* stops when there's nothing new. Then the results go to Google Sheets. Set your own credential and target (sheet ID / channel) on the last node.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "e64a19e0-f9fe-49dc-8e13-bda5158ba2ef",
      "name": "Step 3: Deliver",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
